  <div id="ssr"><article><h1>Cursor+MCP Enables Beginners to Do Blender Renders</h1><p>Star_Knight12 · x · 2026-07-13</p><p>The author recounted opening Blender for the first time by having Cursor&#39;s GPT-5.6 Sol set up Blender MCP. It directly generated a &#34;realistic floating MacBook&#34; and rendered the entire project.</p><p>The highlight isn&#39;t Blender itself, but how the Model + Cursor + MCP + Rendering Tool workflow can empower a complete beginner to execute an end-to-end production pipeline.</p><p><a href="/en/e/19f5609be2748217799dea52292">Related event: Beginner Runs Blender Rendering via Cursor and MCP(9 posts)→</a></p><p><a href="https://x.com/Star_Knight12/status/2076631428926972177" rel="noopener">Original post →</a></p><h2>More from coding &amp; agent</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/p/1a17156a9b7f021c722263639e4">Octopus OS: a 45k-line Rust kernel where agents rewrite their own harness mid-task</a> — _AustinCalvert_ · 2026-10-25</li><li><a href="/en/p/1a17153aa248061a74cff5314a9">Dev argues Rust would be better if modules, not crates, were the compilation unit</a> — zetalyrae · 2026-10-25</li><li><a href="/en/p/1a17155142c9ab63dd3f4a373e2">Dev open-sources BizAgent framework where one AI lead agent manages a dozen AI employees</a> — Low-Start2333 · 2026-10-25</li><li><a href="/en/p/1a1714f4a0e3e005ce5f4d3c285">Formal Verification Yields to Static Analysis, Which Yields to Better Language Design</a> — xennygrimmato_ · 2026-10-25</li><li><a href="/en/p/1a171551795cf3c3b4e08890e58">Scanning 115,798 agent ledger rows: zero capability revocations, none with expiry</a> — Affectionate-Sun265 · 2026-10-25</li><li><a href="/en/p/1a1714188a4c4534fb892745ec2">&#39;Slurm&#39;s defense remains annoyingly strong&#39;: dev watches agents hit HPC wall</a> — sloppenheimer · 2026-10-25</li></ul><p><a href="/en/c/coding-agents">coding &amp; agent channel →</a></p></article></div><script>document.getElementById("ssr").remove()</script>
